\caption(A correctly converged conditional mode can still miss skew posterior moments; the larger-sample sequence checks how that discrepancy changes.)
\alttext(Left: direct finite-window Bernoulli posterior and its local Gaussian approximation. Right: absolute mean and SD differences at 4, 20, 100 and 400 observations, with success fraction three quarters.)

>> Unknown precision: integrate conditional normals rather than only their mode

Return to \(y=(1,2,3)\) with unit observation noise, but now use
\(x\mid\theta\sim N(0,e^{-\theta})\) and \(\theta\sim N(0,1)\).
The fitted theta coordinate is **log precision**. Its prior is already a density on
that scale; substituting a prior density for precision itself would require a Jacobian.
We restrict the numerical integration box to [-6,6], where the standard-normal prior
has negligible omitted mass, and use a five-curvature-SD grid span.

At each theta the exact conditional variance is \(v_k=(3+e^{\theta_k})^{-1}\)
and mean is \(m_k=6v_k\). Thus conditional Gaussian approximation error vanishes
in this example. The remaining difference from the full posterior comes from mode
search and numerical hyperparameter integration. EB freezes \(\theta\) at its
selected mode. The integrated marginal can be skew even though every component is
normal; replacing it with a normal having the final mean and SD would lose that shape.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/inla_precision_mixture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace b               = dm::bayes;
  using M                   = dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double>;
  const auto     likelihood = b::inla_gaussian_likelihood([](const auto&) { return 1.; });
  const auto     precision  = [](const auto& t) { return M(1, 1, std::exp(t[0])); };
  const auto     prior      = [](const auto& t) { return b::normal_lpdf(t[0], 0, 1); };
  b::INLAOptions o;
  o.grid_points_per_dim  = 31;
  o.grid_span            = 5;
  o.mode_population_size = 20;
  o.mode_max_generations = 80;
  const auto grid =
      b::INLA(o).fit(M(3, 1, 1), {1, 2, 3}, likelihood, precision, prior, {-6}, {6}, {0});
  o.strategy = b::INLAIntegrationStrategy::EmpiricalBayes;
  const auto eb =
      b::INLA(o).fit(M(3, 1, 1), {1, 2, 3}, likelihood, precision, prior, {-6}, {6}, {0});
  const auto x          = dm::seql(-1, 4, 501).values();
  const auto density    = b::inla_latent_density(grid, 0, x),
             eb_density = b::inla_latent_density(eb, 0, x), table = b::inla_grid_table(grid);
  std::vector<double> theta_density;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < table.nrows(); ++i)
    theta_density.push_back(table.double_at("weight", i) / table.double_at("cell_volume", i));
  auto theta =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .line(table.numeric_column("theta_0").values(), theta_density, "", {40, 100, 190})
          .title("Weighted log-precision grid")
          .x_label("theta = log precision")
          .y_label("approximate theta density");
  auto latent = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                    .line(x, density.numeric_column("density").values(), "Grid", {40, 100, 190})
                    .line(x, eb_density.numeric_column("density").values(), "EB", {190, 100, 35})
                    .title("Latent marginal after mixing")
                    .x_label("latent mean x")
                    .y_label("density")
                    .x_limits(-1, 4)
                    .y_limits(0, 1.1)
                    .legend({"Grid", "EB"}, {{40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}});
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(theta).add(latent).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/inla_precision_mixture.svg");
  const auto summaries =
      b::inla_latent_summary(grid)
          .mutate("strategy", std::vector<std::string>{"Grid"})
          .concat_rows(
              b::inla_latent_summary(eb).mutate("strategy", std::vector<std::string>{"EB"}));
  std::print(
      "Moment decomposition\n\n{}\n\nGrid theta mean={:.9f}, SD={:.9f}, log evidence={:.9f}; EB "
      "integrated evidence={}.\n\nRetained grid\n\n{}\n",
      summaries.to_md(6),
      grid.theta_mean[0],
      grid.theta_sd[0],
      grid.log_marginal_likelihood,
      eb.log_marginal_likelihood,
      table.to_md(6));
}
```
