\caption(The grid exposes the hyperparameter weights, exact conditional Gaussian moments and additional variance from mixing their locations.)
\alttext(Left: approximate log-precision posterior density from normalized cell weights divided by cell widths. Right: the integrated latent Gaussian mixture versus its empirical-Bayes single component. The table splits total variance into within and between terms.)

> Checking integration resolution

Refine the same Gaussian-conditional model from 7 to 15, 31 and 61 grid points per
axis. A final 61-point calculation increases the span from five to seven curvature
SDs, checking a truncation effect that resolution at a fixed span can miss. We
report the actual retained count, theta moments, latent moments, evidence,
outer-grid edge mass and skipped candidates. Similar values after refinement are
useful numerical evidence; a small edge mass is not a rigorous tail bound and can
miss a binding integration box. In the observed-data example we therefore vary
prior support separately. No grid setting is selected by test-label accuracy.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/inla_grid_refinement.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace b = dm::bayes;
  using M     = dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double>;
  std::vector<double> points, span, retained, mean, sd, theta_mean, theta_sd, evidence, edge,
      skipped;
  for (const auto& setting :
       std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, double>>{{7, 5}, {15, 5}, {31, 5}, {61, 5}, {61, 7}}) {
    const auto     count = setting.first;
    b::INLAOptions o;
    o.grid_points_per_dim  = count;
    o.grid_span            = setting.second;
    o.mode_population_size = 20;
    o.mode_max_generations = 80;
    const auto f           = b::INLA(o).fit(
        M(3, 1, 1),
        {1, 2, 3},
        b::inla_gaussian_likelihood([](const auto&) { return 1.; }),
        [](const auto& t) { return M(1, 1, std::exp(t[0])); },
        [](const auto& t) { return b::normal_lpdf(t[0], 0, 1); },
        {-6},
        {6},
        {0});
    points.push_back(count);
    span.push_back(setting.second);
    retained.push_back(f.theta_grid_weights.size());
    mean.push_back(f.latent_mean[0]);
    sd.push_back(f.latent_sd[0]);
    theta_mean.push_back(f.theta_mean[0]);
    theta_sd.push_back(f.theta_sd[0]);
    evidence.push_back(f.log_marginal_likelihood);
    edge.push_back(f.grid_edge_mass);
    skipped.push_back(f.grid_skipped_points);
  }
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame table;
  table.add_column("axis_points", points);
  table.add_column("span", span);
  table.add_column("retained", retained);
  table.add_column("latent_mean", mean);
  table.add_column("latent_sd", sd);
  table.add_column("theta_mean", theta_mean);
  table.add_column("theta_sd", theta_sd);
  table.add_column("log_evidence", evidence);
  table.add_column("grid_edge_mass", edge);
  table.add_column("skipped", skipped);
  auto moments = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                     .line(points, mean, "mean", {40, 100, 190})
                     .points(points, mean, "", {40, 100, 190}, 5)
                     .line(points, sd, "SD", {190, 100, 35})
                     .points(points, sd, "", {190, 100, 35}, 5)
                     .title("Latent moments under refinement")
                     .x_label("grid points per axis")
                     .y_label("latent-coordinate units")
                     .y_limits(0, 2.2)
                     .legend({"mean", "SD"}, {{40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}});
  std::vector<double> evidence_difference;
  for (double v : evidence)
    evidence_difference.push_back(1000 * (v - evidence.back()));
  auto integral = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                      .line(points, evidence_difference, "", {40, 100, 190})
                      .points(points, evidence_difference, "", {40, 100, 190}, 5)
                      .title("Log evidence relative to wider grid")
                      .x_label("grid points per axis")
                      .y_label("1000 x log-evidence difference");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(moments)
      .add(integral)
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/inla_grid_refinement.svg");
  std::print("{}\n", table.to_md(6));
}
```
